{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488281-forces-6-doubles-the-effectiveness-of-the-sphere","id":1488281,"title":"Forces 6 doubles the effectiveness of the Sphere?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-28T13:39:08-07:00","id":1488281,"title":"Forces 6 doubles the effectiveness of the Sphere?","content":"I was reading the contentious Masters of the Art one of these days and I read the description for Forces 6, did I understand it right? Does it basically doubles the successes one have in like damage tables and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:51:07-07:00","id":1488345,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's a Mastery sphere and walking off into plot point powers. What makes the Masters of the Art contentious? (Beyond the fact that it's out of scope for 99% of all Mage campaigns ever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T12:01:25-07:00","id":1488377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488281-forces-6-doubles-the-effectiveness-of-the-sphere?p=1488345#post1488345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It's a Mastery sphere and walking off into plot point powers. What makes the Masters of the Art contentious? (Beyond the fact that it's out of scope for 99% of all Mage campaigns ever).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, beyond the fact that I heard it was a flop, many people simply ignore it and/or make many critics to the powers. Specially because many doesn't seem to improve much what the Spheres already can do, there's a feel like it was somehow rushed to just fill the points between 6-10, etc. There's also the fact that one of the writers said archspheres was a typo or something, I don't recall it very well, but I remember seeing something along those lines, that Spheres didn't need to go to level &quot;10&quot;. In any case, most people I know prefer Horizon's approach to archspheres, i.e. level 6 being the highest and allowing for &quot;great works&quot;, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T14:07:11-07:00","id":1488391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488281-forces-6-doubles-the-effectiveness-of-the-sphere?p=1488377#post1488377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, beyond the fact that I heard it was a flop, many people simply ignore it and/or make many critics to the powers. Specially because many doesn't seem to improve much what the Spheres already can do, there's a feel like it was somehow rushed to just fill the points between 6-10, etc. There's also the fact that one of the writers said archspheres was a typo or something, I don't recall it very well, but I remember seeing something along those lines, that Spheres didn't need to go to level &quot;10&quot;. In any case, most people I know prefer Horizon's approach to archspheres, i.e. level 6 being the highest and allowing for &quot;great works&quot;, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, Sphere's don't need to go to 10. That's quite correct. Mind you, the rest of the book ain't that bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T14:22:36-07:00","id":1488393,"title":"","content":"I believe the issue is that there's a difference between being poorly received and being contentious. Contentious implies something about the book that inspires division among the fans. If most of the fans think the book isn't worth using, it's not contentious even if the community is largely negative towards it.<br /> <br /> The typo thing is a reference to a different book (aka the first time a character was printed with a Sphere rated at 6), which lead to fans wanting to see archmages as people with 6+ ratings in Spheres instead of a looser term for mages of sufficient age and skill to have mastered multiple Spheres with the Arete to put them to use beyond what most mages will ever manage.<br /> <br /> The bigger issue of contention isn't really MotA specifically, but the three competing official models for how to handle archmages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T14:53:25-07:00","id":1488394,"title":"","content":"My own preference is to not even use the sixth dot for Effects: stick to 5, and represent archmastery-level Effects through Outlandish or Godlike Feats (requiring 10 or more successes, and with an additional +1 to +3 Difficulty). <br /> <br /> One of the lessons of Mastery of the Arts is that the game systems start to break down once you start getting into the 6+ Sphere range. Even at Mastery, the difficulties of Coincidental and Vulgar Effects are 8 and 9, respectively. With the Archspheres, even a Coincidental Effect has a difficulty of at least 9; and by the time you get to nine dots in a Sphere (the highest that Masters of the Art goes), the <i>lowest</i> you can bring the difficulty, even with the maximum reduction possible from Magickal Modifiers, is 9. Unless you use the Threshold system (which essentially boils down to \u201creplace difficulties above 9 with a requirement for more successes\u201d), Archmagic is effectively impossible even for Archmasters. <br /> <br /> When I allow 6 or more dots <i>at all</i>, I'm more inclined to simply have each dot over 5 reduce the number of successes needed for the Effect to work. So with a sixth dot, you can perform a Standard Feat (2 successes) as if it was a Simple Feat (1 success), or a Difficult Feat (3 successes) as if it was a Standard Feat (2 successes). I'd escalate this, with the seventh dot reducing the required successes by 2 (for a total reduction of 3 successes), the eighth dot removing three successes from the requirement (for a total reduction of 6 successes), and the ninth dot removing four successes (for a total reduction of 10 successes). I might even implement a reverse of the Threshold rule, where reductions below a Simple Feat (one success) instead start reducing the target number. <br /> <br /> So nine dots in a Sphere would let you perform a Godlike Feat as if it was \u201cmerely\u201d Outlandish, an Outlandish Feat as if it was Simple, Standard, Difficult, Impressive, or Mighty, and anything not Outlandish or Godlike (that is, 10 or less required successes) as if it were Simple. This, combined with the fact that you'd have an Arete pool of 9 or 10 dice, makes the Archmaster incredibly powerful, as there are Effects that would be Great Works even to a regular Master that the Archmaster could manage as a Rite or even as a basic casting; and using the Automatic Successes optional rules, the Archmaster might not even need to roll. In short, Archspheres wouldn't open more doors for the Archmaster (because the Archmaster can already do pretty much anything with the Sphere); instead, they would make what he can already do even easier. <br /> <br /> So when an <i>Archmaster</i> breaks out the Ceremony or Great Work, you know that something truly <i>epic</i> is going down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T14:55:14-07:00","id":1488395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488281-forces-6-doubles-the-effectiveness-of-the-sphere?p=1488393#post1488393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the issue is that there's a difference between being poorly received and being contentious. Contentious implies something about the book that inspires division among the fans. If most of the fans think the book isn't worth using, it's not contentious even if the community is largely negative towards it.<br /> <br /> The typo thing is a reference to a different book (aka the first time a character was printed with a Sphere rated at 6), which lead to fans wanting to see archmages as people with 6+ ratings in Spheres instead of a looser term for mages of sufficient age and skill to have mastered multiple Spheres with the Arete to put them to use beyond what most mages will ever manage.<br /> <br /> The bigger issue of contention isn't really MotA specifically, but the three competing official models for how to handle archmages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three? I know there's Horizon and Masters of the Art; what's the third?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T16:46:45-07:00","id":1488408,"title":"","content":"The original intent of lots of Spheres and Arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}